Subject: [PATCH] tests: fix test_json_parse_cli portability

test_json_parse_cli.test is a /bin/sh script but relies on two things that
are not portable, and both make the test fail in a minimal build
environment:

1. `echo -n` is not POSIX. Under a /bin/sh whose echo lacks -n (dash), the
   literal "-n " is written to file1.dat along with a trailing newline.
   json_parse then chokes on the leading "-" ("offset 1: number expected")
   and every byte offset is shifted, so the expected output never matches.
   `printf '%s'` writes the string with no newline on every shell.

2. `echo 'e2' | xxd -r -p` appends a bare 0xE2 byte (a truncated 3-byte
   UTF-8 sequence) so that json_parse rejects the input. `xxd` ships with
   vim and is not present in a minimal build environment, so the command
   fails, file2.dat ends up without the invalid byte, and json_parse exits
   0 instead of 1. `printf '\342'` is POSIX and emits the identical byte.

With both fixed the test produces the committed
tests/test_json_parse_cli.expected output and exits 1 as intended.

diff --git a/tests/test_json_parse_cli.test b/tests/test_json_parse_cli.test
index 0982afe..0f7796c 100755
--- a/tests/test_json_parse_cli.test
+++ b/tests/test_json_parse_cli.test
@@ -10,8 +10,8 @@ fi
 
 set -x -v
 
-echo -n '"tenant=blue;note=CANARY_STACK_WINDOW_2026;status=ok"' > file1.dat
-(printf '"' ; printf 'A%.0s' $(seq 1 16) ; echo 'e2'  | xxd -r -p) > file2.dat
+printf '%s' '"tenant=blue;note=CANARY_STACK_WINDOW_2026;status=ok"' > file1.dat
+(printf '"' ; printf 'A%.0s' $(seq 1 16) ; printf '\342') > file2.dat
 
 TESTNAME="${0##*/}"
 TESTNAME="${TESTNAME%.test}"
